{
  "$comment": "#FEED-232 (owner 2026-11-12: 'one system with numbers that is consistent and logical ... everywhere'). ONE COUNT BADGE ×4 (+ the genUI `CountBadge`, React · Solid · Swift · Compose · gpui): every unread / attention signal on a destination (a sidebar row, a phone tab, the Inbox circle, a chat-list row, the team picker, the OS app icon) is a NUMBER = the items in that destination needing the viewer, drawn by THE count badge: a 16pt capsule (min width 16, 4pt side padding), 10pt semibold tabular figures, `label(count)` = the number, `99+` past 99, and ZERO OR LESS = NO BADGE (`labelCases`, `''` = nothing renders). TWO TONES, nothing else: `attention` (the needs-you yellow #FACC15, black figures) when the count holds an item WAITING ON the viewer (a plan, a question, a ready PR, a session parked on input), else `muted` (muted fill, muted-foreground figures) for plain unread. No dots: a dot never stands for a count. LIVE STATE IS NOT A COUNT: `running` / busy never badges a nav row (no green dot anywhere in the nav); it lives on the rows themselves (the working mark of a chat / run row, the Running section). WHAT EACH DESTINATION COUNTS (one definition each): NEEDS YOU = needs-you.json rows' length, always `attention`. CHATS (sidebar row, phone Chats tab) = `chatsBadge(groups, reads)` (`chatsCases`): the DISTINCT depth-0 chat rows (a session counted once across groups) that need the viewer or hold an unread reply, an archived root counting only while it needs the viewer; child rows never; `attention` when one of them needs the viewer. AN AGENT ROW (sidebar Agents, the pinned agent / app rows of the Chats list) and A CHAT-LIST ROW = `rowBadge({unreadCount, needsYou})` (`rowCases`): the row's unread agent messages (chats.json `unreadCount`), at least 1 while it needs the viewer, `attention` when it does; a busy row with nothing unread = no badge (its run mark shows the work). INBOX (the wide Inbox button, the phone page header's Inbox circle) = the active team's unread notifications the inbox can show, `muted`. DRAFTS = the team's drafts, `muted`. DEVICES, APPS, BOARDS, PINS = no badge. THE TEAM PICKER (the switcher's corner + each OTHER team's row; the active team never) = that team's needs-you rows' length, `attention`; the switcher corner = `appIconBadge` over the other teams. THE OS APP ICON (iOS `setBadgeCount`, Android the summary notification's number, web `navigator.setAppBadge` where supported, desktop the dock / launcher entry) = `appIconBadge(teams)` (`appIconCases`): the SUM of every team's needs-you rows of the signed-in account(s), 0 clears it. Mirrors: TS src/nav-badges.ts, desktop domain::nav_badges, iOS ExpCore NavBadges.swift, Android domain/NavBadges.kt; each replays every case list.",
